# Part Four — The Index of Laws

> The articles of the Constitution, every Pakistani law on women with its key provisions and sections, and the international instruments Pakistan has accepted. The **Topic** column shows where each is taught.

## 4.1  The Constitution of Pakistan, 1973 — articles on women

::: table | Constitutional articles that matter for Gender Studies.
@widths 2.2,9.8,2
@font 9.5
Article | What it says | Topic
8 | Laws inconsistent with fundamental rights are void | T5
9 | Security of person — no one deprived of life or liberty save by law | T5, T7
11 | Slavery, forced labour and trafficking prohibited | T5, T7
14 | Dignity of man and privacy of home inviolable | T5, T7
17 | Freedom of association; right to form or join political parties | T6
25 | Equality before law; no discrimination on the basis of sex; special provision for women and children allowed (25(3)) | T5, T6, T7
25A | Free and compulsory education for children aged 5–16 (18th Amendment, 2010) | T5
26–27 | No discrimination in access to public places or in public service on the basis of sex | T5
32 | Representation of women in local government | T5, T6
34 | Steps to ensure full participation of women in all spheres of national life | T5, T6
35 | Protection of marriage, the family, the mother and the child | T5, T7
37(e) | Just and humane conditions of work; maternity benefits for women in employment | T5
51, 59, 106 | Reserved seats for women in the National Assembly, Senate and provincial assemblies | T6
:::

Fundamental rights (Articles 8–28) are enforceable in court; the Principles of Policy (Articles 29–40, including 32, 34, 35 and 37) are goals of the state, not directly enforceable.

## 4.2  Pakistan's laws on women — chronological

::: table | Pakistani laws on women and gender, with key provisions.
@widths 1.4,4.4,6.6,1.6
@font 9
Year | Law | Key provisions | Topic
1860 | Pakistan Penal Code | Murder, hurt, rape (from 2006), s. 509 insult to modesty; "grave and sudden provocation" | T7
1890 | Guardians and Wards Act | Custody and guardianship; child's welfare paramount | T5
1929 | Child Marriage Restraint Act | Minimum age (girls raised to 16 by MFLO 1961) | T5, T7
1937 | Muslim Personal Law (Shariat) Application Act | Islamic personal law for Muslims (agricultural land added in Punjab, 1948) | T5
1939 | Dissolution of Muslim Marriages Act | Grounds for judicial divorce by the wife | T5
1961 | Muslim Family Laws Ordinance | Marriage registration; polygamy needs Arbitration Council permission; *talaq* notice, effective after 90 days; orphaned grandchildren inherit | T3, T5
1964 | Family Courts Act | Special family courts | T5
1976 | Dowry and Bridal Gifts (Restriction) Act | Limits on dowry; rarely enforced | T5, T7
1979 | Hudood Ordinances (Zina Ordinance) | Rape victims risked adultery charges; four-witness rule | T3, T5, T7
1981 | Disabled Persons (Employment and Rehabilitation) Ordinance | Job quota for persons with disabilities | T5
1984 | Qanun-e-Shahadat (Law of Evidence) | Evidence of two women equal to one man in certain financial matters | T3
1990/1997 | Qisas and Diyat Ordinance / Act | Murder compoundable; heirs may forgive — the honour-killing loophole | T5, T7
2001 | Local Government Ordinance | 33% of council seats for women | T6
2002 | Legal Framework Order (validated by 17th Amendment, 2003) | 60 NA, 17 Senate, 128 provincial seats for women; NA of 342 | T6
2004 | Criminal Law (Amendment) Act | Honour crimes defined (*karo-kari*); penalties raised | T5, T7
2006 | Protection of Women (Criminal Laws Amendment) Act | Rape moved from the Zina Ordinance to the Penal Code; no four-witness rule for rape | T3, T5, T7
2010 | Protection against Harassment of Women at the Workplace Act (amended 2022) | Inquiry committees; code of conduct; ombudspersons | T5, T7
2010 | Criminal Law (Amendment) Act — s. 509 PPC | Harassment in public places: up to 3 years and fine | T7
2010 | 18th Amendment | Art. 25A; devolution of women's development, health and education to provinces | T5, T6
2011 | Acid Control and Acid Crime Prevention Act | ss. 336A–336B PPC: 14 years to life; fine at least Rs 1 million | T5, T7
2011 | Prevention of Anti-Women Practices Act | s. 310A *vani*/*swara*; s. 498A denial of inheritance; s. 498B forced marriage; s. 498C marriage to the Qur'an | T5, T7
2012 | National Commission on the Status of Women Act; NCHR Act | Statutory commissions | T5, T6
2013 | Sindh Child Marriages Restraint Act | Minimum marriage age 18 for both sexes | T5
2013 | Sindh Domestic Violence (Prevention and Protection) Act | First provincial DV law | T5, T7
2014 | Balochistan Domestic Violence (Prevention and Protection) Act | Protection orders | T5, T7
2016 | Punjab Protection of Women against Violence Act | Violence = DV, sexual, psychological, economic abuse, stalking, cybercrime; interim, protection (GPS bracelet), residence and monetary orders; VAW centres | T5, T7
2016 | Criminal Law (Amendment) (Offences in the name or pretext of Honour) Act | Life imprisonment even if the family forgives (MCQ 2026) | T5, T7
2016 | Criminal Law (Amendment) (Offences relating to Rape) Act | DNA testing; in-camera trials; penalties for obstructing investigation | T7
2016 | Prevention of Electronic Crimes Act (amended 2025) | ss. 20–21 dignity and modesty; s. 24 cyber-stalking | T5, T7
2016 | Sindh Hindu Marriage Act | Registration of Hindu marriages | T5
2017 | Hindu Marriage Act (federal) | Registration of Hindu marriages (ICT and other provinces) | T5
2017 | Elections Act | s. 206: 5% of general tickets to women; s. 9: poll void if women's turnout below 10%; registration measures | T6
2018 | Transgender Persons (Protection of Rights) Act | Self-perceived identity; anti-discrimination (FSC 2023; appeal pending) | T1, T7
2018 | Prevention of Trafficking in Persons Act | Trafficking offences | T7
2018 | Sindh Home-Based Workers Act; Sindh Maternity Benefits Act | Rights and minimum wages for home-based workers; maternity benefits | T4, T5
2019 | Punjab Domestic Workers Act | Rights of domestic workers | T5
2020 | Enforcement of Women's Property Rights Act | Complaints to the Ombudsperson on denied inheritance | T4, T5
2020 | Maternity and Paternity Leave Act | Extended maternity leave; paternity leave (federal) | T5
2020 | ICT Rights of Persons with Disability Act | Accessibility; inclusive education | T5
2020 | Zainab Alert, Response and Recovery Act | Rapid response to missing and abused children | T7
2021 | Anti-Rape (Investigation and Trial) Act | Special Sexual Offences Investigation Units; Anti-Rape Crisis Cells; special courts; trial in about 4 months | T7
2021 | KP Domestic Violence against Women (Prevention and Protection) Act | Protection orders | T5, T7
2025 | ICT Child Marriage Restraint Act | Minimum marriage age 18 in Islamabad | T5
2025 | ICT Domestic Violence (Prevention and Protection) Act | Moved by Sharmila Farooqui; NA 13 Nov, Senate 28 Nov | T5, T7
:::

## 4.3  International instruments

::: table | International instruments on women's rights.
@widths 1.4,5,5.8,1.8
@font 9
Year | Instrument | What it does | Pakistan
1948 | Universal Declaration of Human Rights | Art. 21 — right to take part in government | —
1966 | ICCPR | Art. 25 — vote, be elected, public affairs | Ratified 2010
1966 | ICESCR | Economic, social and cultural rights | Ratified 2008
1979 | CEDAW | Art. 4(1) temporary special measures; Art. 7 political life; Art. 16 marriage and family | Acceded 1996 (with a declaration)
1984 | Convention against Torture | Prohibition of torture | Ratified 2010
1989 | Convention on the Rights of the Child | Children's rights | Ratified 1990
1992 | CEDAW General Recommendation 19 | GBV is discrimination | —
1993 | Declaration on the Elimination of Violence against Women | Definition of VAW (Art. 1); three sites (Art. 2) | —
1995 | Beijing Declaration and Platform for Action | 12 critical areas (D violence; G power and decision-making) | Endorsed
2000 | UN Security Council Resolution 1325 | Women, peace and security | —
2006 | Convention on the Rights of Persons with Disabilities | Disability rights | Ratified 2011
2011 | Istanbul Convention (Council of Europe) | Prevention, protection, prosecution, integrated policies | Not a party
2015 | Sustainable Development Goals | Goal 5; targets 5.2 (violence), 5.3 (child marriage), 5.5 (leadership), 5.b (technology) | Adopted by NA 2016
2017 | CEDAW General Recommendation 35 | Updates GR 19 | —
:::
